// KNOWN BUG check.assign_readonly_ref_param: a plain `ref` parameter is a
// read-only borrow; only `var ref` writes back to the caller
// (tests/conformance/memory/var_ref_writeback.pilot). Assigning to a plain
// `ref` parameter is a reassignment of an immutable binding, so the checker
// must reject it (DECL004) before anything runs. Today it is accepted: the
// seed drops the write (prints true, -1) and PilIR stops at the seam
// `ir.lower_construct`. This hid a bug in `std/proc` (`proc_make_pipe`), which
// left every child process writing to the terminal.
fn set_one(ref a: i64) -> bool {
    a = 3;
    return true;
}

fn main() {
    var x = -1;
    print(set_one(x));
    print(x);
}
